      "content": "The museum has a moral imperative to acknowledge the historical injustices inherent in colonial acquisition. Repatriation is not merely a gesture of goodwill, but a necessary act of decolonization that rectifies past wrongs. We must prioritize the cultural sovereignty of source communities over the institutional prestige of holding these objects. Therefore, a commitment to returning these artifacts is the only ethical path forward.",
